item 1 measure is identified by "http://example.org/analysis/assessment/1/1/measure".

item 1 measure is an assessment statement.

item 1 measure has the interpretation "http://data.europa.eu/leg/interop-assessment#InterpretationPositive".

item 1 measure has the judgement "Introduces a streamlined notification-based system enabling providers to operate in one or several Member States on the basis of a single authorisation, thus improving legal interoperability.".

item 1 measure has the statement type "http://data.europa.eu/leg/interop-assessment#StatementTypeAlignmentMeasure".

item 1 measure concerns the service interop 1.

item 1 measure has the description "Alignment with existing digital and sectorial policiesPlease list the applicable digital and sectorial policies identified".


item 2 measure is identified by "http://example.org/analysis/assessment/1/2/measure".

item 2 measure is an assessment statement.

item 2 measure has the interpretation "http://data.europa.eu/leg/interop-assessment#InterpretationPositive".

item 2 measure has the judgement "Under the single passport procedure, it is established that a provider shall submit a notification to the national regulatory authority of one of those Member States where it intends to provide networks or services. Additional data flows are in place to govern how coordination between Member Stated and ODN shall look like.
Each Member State shall designate a national single contact point.
ODN is charged with the maintenance of a central database of all notifications provided in the context of the Single Passport procedure. Competent authorities should transmit only complete notifications to the ODN".

item 2 measure has the statement type "http://data.europa.eu/leg/interop-assessment#StatementTypeOrganisationMeasure".

item 2 measure concerns the service interop 1.

item 2 measure has the description "Organisational measures for a smooth cross-border digital public services deliveryPlease list the governance measures foreseen".


item 3 measure is identified by "http://example.org/analysis/assessment/1/3/measure".

item 3 measure is an assessment statement.

item 3 measure has the interpretation "http://data.europa.eu/leg/interop-assessment#InterpretationPositive".

item 3 measure has the judgement "The notification of intention to provide networks or services shall be made in accordance with a notification template to be made available by BEREC.".

item 3 measure has the statement type "http://data.europa.eu/leg/interop-assessment#StatementTypeSharedMeasure".

item 3 measure concerns the service interop 1.

item 3 measure has the description "Measures taken to ensure a shared understanding of the dataPlease list such measures".


item 4 barrier is identified by "http://example.org/analysis/assessment/1/4/barrier".

item 4 barrier is an assessment statement.

item 4 barrier has the interpretation "http://data.europa.eu/leg/interop-assessment#InterpretationPositive".

item 4 barrier has the judgement "No remaining barriers.".

item 4 barrier has the statement type "http://data.europa.eu/leg/interop-assessment#StatementTypeStandardsBarrier".

item 4 barrier concerns the service interop 1.

item 4 barrier has the description "Use of commonly agreed open technical specifications and standardsPlease list such measures".


item 5 barrier is identified by "http://example.org/analysis/assessment/1/5/barrier".

item 5 barrier is an assessment statement.

item 5 barrier has the interpretation "http://data.europa.eu/leg/interop-assessment#InterpretationPositive".

item 5 barrier has the judgement "No remaining barriers.".

item 5 barrier has the statement type "http://data.europa.eu/leg/interop-assessment#StatementTypeAlignmentBarrier".

item 5 barrier concerns the service interop 2.

item 5 barrier has the description "Alignment with existing digital and sectorial policiesPlease list the applicable digital and sectorial policies identified".


item 6 measure is identified by "http://example.org/analysis/assessment/1/6/measure".

item 6 measure is an assessment statement.

item 6 measure has the interpretation "http://data.europa.eu/leg/interop-assessment#InterpretationPositive".

item 6 measure has the judgement "The ODN shall establish and administer dynamic databases for geolocation and monitoring of spectrum usage opportunities.
The ODN, in cooperation with national regulatory authorities, an under the supervision of BEREC, shall establish and keep an up-to-date the database of the pan-European numbering resources.".

item 6 measure has the statement type "http://data.europa.eu/leg/interop-assessment#StatementTypeOrganisationMeasure".

item 6 measure concerns the service interop 2.

item 6 measure has the description "Organisational measures for a smooth cross-border digital public services deliveryPlease list the governance measures foreseen".


item 7 measure is identified by "http://example.org/analysis/assessment/1/7/measure".

item 7 measure is an assessment statement.

item 7 measure has the interpretation "http://data.europa.eu/leg/interop-assessment#InterpretationPositive".

item 7 measure has the judgement "The Commission, taking utmost account of the views of the RSPB, may adopt implementing acts to define the spectrum bands covered by the dynamic database and develop uniform formats for the collection and provision of data by the competent authorities.
Six months after the adoption of the Union numbering plan, the ODN shall set up the procedure for provision of information that will feed the pan-European numbering resources database.".

item 7 measure has the statement type "http://data.europa.eu/leg/interop-assessment#StatementTypeSharedMeasure".

item 7 measure concerns the service interop 2.

item 7 measure has the description "Measures taken to ensure a shared understanding of the dataPlease list such measures".


item 8 measure is identified by "http://example.org/analysis/assessment/1/8/measure".

item 8 measure is an assessment statement.

item 8 measure has the interpretation "http://data.europa.eu/leg/interop-assessment#InterpretationPositive".

item 8 measure has the judgement "The ODN shall establish technical specifications for the dynamic database for geolocation and monitoring of spectrum usage opportunities, and the pan-European numbering resources database, at a later date.".

item 8 measure has the statement type "http://data.europa.eu/leg/interop-assessment#StatementTypeStandardsMeasure".

item 8 measure concerns the service interop 2.

item 8 measure has the description "Use of commonly agreed open technical specifications and standards".


